# Proof-of-Reality Network — Implementation Plan

> **Goal**: Build a hackathon MVP that lets users upload digital content (video/image/audio), run AI forensic analysis, generate a Reality Score, store the verification on blockchain, and produce a publicly verifiable authenticity certificate.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Monorepo Structure**: The plan uses a single monorepo with three sub-projects (`frontend/`, `backend/`, `blockchain/`). If you'd prefer separate repos or a different folder structure, let me know.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Blockchain Network**: This plan uses **Polygon Amoy Testnet** (Chain ID: 80002, gas token: POL). You'll need a MetaMask wallet and free testnet POL from [Polygon Faucet](https://faucet.polygon.technology/). Confirm this is acceptable.

> [!WARNING]
> **AI Models — Simulated for MVP**: Training/running real EfficientNet deepfake models requires GPU and large datasets. For the hackathon demo, the AI engine will use **realistic simulated analysis** (deterministic scoring based on file properties like metadata, hash entropy, file size, and frame extraction) to demonstrate the full pipeline. This is standard practice for hackathon MVPs — judges evaluate the architecture and workflow, not whether you trained a novel ML model from scratch. The architecture is designed so real models (EfficientNet-B0, MTCNN, etc.) can be dropped in later as a plug-in replacement.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Environment Prerequisites**: You'll need Node.js 18+, Python 3.10+, FFmpeg installed and on PATH, and a MetaMask wallet private key for blockchain deployment. Confirm these are available on your machine.

